  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for pgvector",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for pgvector fixes the following issue:\n\n- CVE-2026-103484: database users with the ability to create an IVFFlat index can write data out-of-bounds, which can\n  lead to arbitrary code execution (bsc#1284129).\n\nChanges for pgvector:\n\n- Updated to version 0.8.7\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
